# Findings

## Major

1. **The OpenCode timeout path can still certify success after the 60-second poll has expired.** The run-wide constraints and ordered work say that expiry must trigger one final fresh diagnostic sample *before failing*. In `wait_opencode_exit`, however, a passing final sample returns success. Make the post-deadline sample diagnostic-only and return failure unconditionally after recording its result. Success must occur only inside the bounded polling loop.
